+### 21.4 Remote GitHub Workspace materialization
+
+Owner: Repository/Platform. Phase: post-P10 D-040 maintenance. The shared
+GitHub transport now covers Repository connections and managed Workspace
+materialization without adding a table or migration. `inspectRepository` and
+`materializeRepository` mint a short-lived RS256 App JWT, exchange an
+Installation token, validate numeric repository/full-name/branch/HEAD pins,
+and compare the recursive tree/blob manifest before and after a shallow
+`execFile` clone. Truncated trees, submodules, LFS pointers, links, special
+files, unsafe paths, malformed blobs, and file/byte quota overruns fail closed.
+
+`GithubRepositoryAdapter` accepts only the current actor's available GitHub
+profile and active Vault credential. Local Git and fixture sources continue to
+use their existing adapters. Workspace create and refresh materialize into a
+temporary sibling, publish only after hash verification, remove `.git`, retain
+the previous successful copy on refresh failure, reject locked or active-
+execution refreshes, and preserve shared Operation/Event/revision/CAS retry
+lineage. The additive test is
+`tests/p10/remote-workspace-auth.test.mjs`; maintenance Evidence is append-only
+under `docs/evidence/post-p10-development-reliability-20260905/` and does not
+promote a Catalog row.
